------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAMESPACE NOTE (collision detected + resolved within allowed files)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  An existing dashboard-widget (TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/VehicleHeroCardWidget.*) already owns the
  bare `VehicleHero*` type-name namespace (VehicleHeroModel/Connection/Status/Source/Telemetry/
  Projection/Format/Strings/Accessibility/…). To stay additive and NOT edit files outside the allowed
  set, every supporting type this surface declares is prefixed `VehicleHeroPanel*` (the public view
  stays `VehicleHero`, surface slug stays "VehicleHero", strings table stays "VehicleHero", files stay
  VehicleHero.*). This removed the "ambiguous for type lookup" errors from BOTH this surface AND the
  pre-existing VehicleHeroCardWidget (which now compiles clean again).
  The isolated harness additionally surfaced — and this change fixed — a real SwiftUI shadowing bug:
  the free `accentColor(_:)` helper was bound to `View.accentColor(Color?)` inside view bodies; it is
  now namespaced as `VehicleHeroPanelPalette.color(_:)` / `.tone(_:)`.

